    "updated_at": "2026-08-23T06:21:14Z",
    "body": "Hi @linyueqian — I'd like to take **Mechanism 2 (capacity-adaptive, punctuation-aware segmentation)** from this RFC, plus its ρ instrumentation prerequisite (a mergeable observability-only first PR on the async-chunk ramp path in `qwen3_tts_code2wav.py`).\n\nPlan: segmentation policy engine as a model-agnostic module with CPU unit tests (ρ̂ via EMA + static-ramp warmup, budget freeze at segment open, punctuation-ranked cuts with a hard-cut ceiling, fragmentation ≤ 1.43× optimal), wired into the live path once #6515/#1766 land — targeting regressions #4913 and #5889.\n\nNo overlap with @liuyao0322's #6515 (commitment policy — different joint: text-release safety vs decode-capacity budgeting). Could you assign me for this slice, or should I just open a draft PR?\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
