    "created_at": "2026-08-23T09:44:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-23T09:44:41Z",
    "body": "Thanks for putting this together — concept ACK. A few points to tighten before interfaces are frozen:\n\n1. Please distinguish transport text chunks, TTS text segments, and codec/audio chunks. `codec_chunk_ramp` controls Talker → Code2Wav output cadence; it is not the CAPS text segmenter. I would define ρ and capacity at Stage 0/Talker using normalized TTS tokens, acoustic output steps, and Talker KV positions.\n2. Reuse the existing `/v1/audio/speech/stream` surface if possible. It already accepts `input.text` but buffers until `input.done`; the missing contract is opt-in early synthesis, backpressure, EOF, cancellation, and compatibility semantics.\n3. Code2Wav currently clears request state on `is_segment_finished`. Cross-segment inheritance needs a logical stream identity, segment sequence, health checks, and terminal/error cleanup. Talker H=4 history is separate, model-specific work.\n4. The related-bug claims should stay narrow: #4913 is primarily output cadence/compute (#5152), while #5889 supports normalization work but its complete-request EOS failure would not be fixed by commitment alone.\n\nSuggested order: contract + CPU commitment tests → live WebSocket integration → Stage-0 ρ instrumentation/CAPS → Code2Wav and Talker inheritance with E2E metrics. Draft #6515 looks like a reasonable first slice.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
